president biden is due to speak with  russian president vladimir putin this  morning the high stakes video call  follows groin concern over russia's  increased military presence on its  border with ukraine last night mr biden  contacted key nato allies to discuss  de-escalating tensions ed o'keefe is at  the white house ed good morning  nate good morning u.s officials stressed  they have no evidence that russian  president putin is actually preparing  for a military invasion but they say the  president is going to raise concerns  about military buildup there between the  border of russia and ukraine there are  several subjects of conversation for  this call not only the threat of a  military invasion but also concerns  about cyber security and construction of  a key gas pipeline from russia into  europe as for potential military action  u.s officials say the president will  tell putin quote there will be real  costs and that diplomacy can resolve the  dispute the u.s is threatening potential  sanctions but officials didn't offer  specifics nor did they make any  commitments to send american troops but  instead promised military support for  ukraine if necessary  ahead of the call putin's spokesman said  the russian leader will once again  insist that ukraine not become a member  of nato and demand guarantees that the  alliance will not expand further east  into former soviet territory senior  administration officials say president  biden believes every country should make  its own security decisions putin's  spokesman described russia's  relationship with the u.s as quote in a  very dire situation  all right we'll be watching and as  always thank you my friend appreciate it
 

